{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Who came from his thigh, besides the wives of Jacob's sons.</b> That is, they are those who came from his thigh, according to the opinion of our Rabbis of blessed memory, who said that twin sisters were born with each of the tribes, and the tribes married their sisters — for what reason would Scripture say <b>besides the wives of Jacob's sons</b>, the Canaanite women? Rather, they too were those who came from his thigh, but Scripture did not make them known. And as for his stating sixty-six: the four were not among those who came, for they were in Egypt — they are Joseph, Manasseh, Ephraim, and Jochebed, of whom it is written (Numbers 26:59): אשר ילדה אותה ללוי במצרים — 'whom she bore to Levi in Egypt.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:45.178209071Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}